  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Winterization Assistance to the Most Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Populations in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the invasion of Ukraine on 24 February 2022, the humanitarian situation in the country quickly deteriorated. As of 23 June, nearly 6.3 million continue to be displaced according to round six of IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Report. Vulnerable populations face increasing protection risks while harsh weather conditions during the upcoming winter season are increasing cause of concern. Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to the protection of the most vulnerable populations in Ukraine including by mitigating the adverse impact of harsh weather conditions. In addition to providing protection services, IOM is building local protection capacities while raising awareness on the availability of such as well as other types of assistance. To mitigate the impact of harsh weather conditions, IOM is providing individual shelter assistance with the aim to repair homes that were damaged by the war, while rehabilitating and upgrading collective centres for populations who continue to be displaced. Additionally, IOM is providing winterized non-food items and core winter clothing.</narrative>
  </description>
